# requirements.in — direct (top-level) dependencies, hand-edited.
#
# requirements.txt is GENERATED from this file and is the fully-pinned lock
# (every transitive included). Regenerate after editing this file with:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.11 -o requirements.txt
#
# --universal emits environment markers so the single lock is valid across OS/arch
# and Python 3.11+ (CI runs Linux on 3.11 and 3.12); --python-version sets the floor.
# CI itself needs no uv — it just runs `pip install -r requirements.txt`.

# 1.5.1: what the bot actually runs, and the version every schwab-py API fact in
# the Phase 0 / Phase 1 design docs was verified against (get_order,
# get_orders_for_account, cancel_order, equity_sell_limit, and the status enum
# spelling CANCELED with one L plus a literal UNKNOWN member).
